==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|highway-robbery}}, {{l|en|highwayrobbery}}

===Etymology===
From {{compound|highway|robbery|lang=en}}. Compare {{etyl|ang|-}} {{term|weġrēaf||highway robbery|lit=road-theft|lang=ang}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=[[highway]] [[robbery]]|highway robberies}}

# {{context|literally|historical|lang=en}} The act of [[rob]]bing a [[traveler]] on a public road.
# {{context|idiomatic|lang=en}} Said of [[excessive]] or [[exorbitant]] prices.
#: ''They think they can charge $400 for a shirt? That's '''highway robbery'''.''

